{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[hæmophilia]]
* [[hemophilia]]

===Etymology===
Medical term; from {{etyl|grc|en}} [[αἷμα]] ([[blood]]) + [[φιλία]] ([[friendship]])

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪliə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{pathology}} Any of several hereditary illnesses that impair the body's ability to control bleeding, usually passed from mother to son.

====Synonyms====
* [[bleeder's disease]]
* [[Christmas disease]]

====Derived terms====
* [[haemophiliac]]
* [[haemophilic]]
* [[haemophile]]

